{color:#0747a6}_Further to our email below, please be informed that our firm's representative was at the Mabushi Police Division in respect of the invitation extended to Bolt by the police investigation team in respect of the above-captioned matter._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_At the Division, we met with the Divisional Police Officer (DPO) in charge of the division and the Investigative Police Officer (IPO) detailed to investigate the matter. The IPO explained that the Police invited Bolt to shed more light on the facts of the matter to enable the Police to get further investigation leads to advance the progress of the investigation._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_We explained to the Police that the driver briefly visited Bolt's Abuja office at Kojo Motors Plaza to resolve an issue on his driver profile. We highlighted that since the issue being resolved was a minor one, the driver spent 15 minutes total in Bolt's office before taking his leave. Therefore, Bolt's staff were equally surprised when the driver came back to state that his vehicle had been stolen._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_Having heard Bolt's side of events, the Police thanked Bolt for its cooperation in respect of the matter. The IPO subsequently stated that, in the circumstances of the unfortunate incident, it would be a welcome gesture if Bolt could support the driver with any monetary token it could muster, since the driver is registered on Bolt's platform and the incident happened when the driver visited Bolt's office. We stated that we would take the Police's comment under advisement and let them know Bolt's stance on the matter._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_In the circumstances, we would continue to update Bolt if any matter arises in the course of the investigation which requires Bolt's attention._{color}

