Hi [~accountid:712020:29d8b602-d17f-40cd-9cae-5653bc2c54b7]! Regarding the T&Cs update timeline, please note the following:

* the works are generally fairly advanced, however, there are still some dependencies that need to be resolved before we proceed further (mainly tax and some discussions with the external counsel who is advising us on this);
* as a next step, the entire text needs to be translated into Slovak (we can do a machine translation, but then it needs to be verified by the local counsel);
* we need at least 15 days after the publication of the T&Cs before they enter into force.

Taking into account the above, it is difficult to commit to a specific short deadline, as simply it is beyond our control, whether we will be able to comply with it or not. I would suggest to give 15 November to the NBS as a date from which the new T&Cs will be applicable. I will be off first two weeks of November, so I will aim to finalize everything until the end of October. Hopefully this will give us a sufficient buffer in case of any delays. 



The explanation that you may offer to the authority on why the deadline is not earlier:

* we are fully committed to ensuring compliance with legal requirements and are actively working on implementing this as soon as possible;
* this is a project coordinated globally that involves many different teams working on it (legal - internal and external, finance, tax, billing and local operations teams);
* the services are provided by the Estonian entity that involves confirmation on a number of matters with the team in Estonia;
* as the new T&Cs will be based on the global template, they need to be translated into Slovak, which also impacts the timeline.

Hope the above is helpful.
Thank you!

