Thank you for your data subject request, which was received by us on *26 August 2025,* where you requested the following:



# A copy of all recorded personal data for your Bolt Drive trip from 24 August 2025 (Invoice no. EE-1235-1016084);
# A method description how your personal data was processed to determine your driving score.





*Response to the first request*



We are attaching a copy of all recorded personal data for your requested Bolt Drive trip, including all recorded raw data values of all data points that were used to determine your driving score. The files include:



* Geolocation and speed data;
* Events log; and
* Vehicle sensor data recording the events contributing to your driving score.





*Response to the second request*



Your driving score is based on the car sensor data during your active order. The sensors record how the car was driven during your trip. We recorded two events:



# Harsh braking;
# Harsh cornering.



We start from 100 points and then subtract a small amount for every harsh event. The deduction depends on the number of events and distance driven. In short, your score shows how smoothly the car was driven. Fewer harsh events during longer distances lead to a higher score.



As you may be aware, the right of access under data protection law does not provide an individual with an absolute right of full access to any and all documents containing their personal data. For example, that right should not adversely affect the rights of others, including our trade secrets or intellectual property and in particular the copyright protecting the software. Due to security reasons and prevention of score manipulation, we are unable to provide a full breakdown of the calculation, coefficients, or detailed thresholds used. We aim to provide sufficient transparency to help you understand how your driving influenced your score while safeguarding our proprietary methods.



For information on how we process relevant personal data, we refer you to our Privacy Notice at [https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/|smart-link] , which includes further information about:

* The categories of personal data we process;
* The purposes for which we process personal data;
* The recipients or categories of recipients to whom the personal data has been or will be disclosed;
* The criteria we use to determine how long to retain personal data;
* The sources of personal data received from other parties;
* Your rights in relation to your personal data;
* The existence and envisaged consequences of any automated decision-making/profiling of personal data; and
* Details of any transfer of your personal data to third countries or international organisations and the safeguards used for any such transfers.



*Your rights* 



In addition to your right to access any personal data we hold about you, you have the right to request us to rectify, erase your personal data, restrict the processing of your personal data or to object to such processing. Any such requests that are received will be considered in conjunction with the applicable provisions of relevant data protection laws. 



If you are dissatisfied with this response to your request or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection/supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.

 

If you have any additional questions, please contact our Customer Support Team by replying to this email.





Yours sincerely,



Bolt{quote}

